Root cause:
The bug was caused by the use of the host PKRU (Page Protect Read/Write/Userspace) value in the `vcpu->arch.guest_fpu.state`, which was restored immediately after the virtual CPU exited. As a result, when retrieving the state using `KVM_GET_XSAVE`, it returned the host's PKRU value instead of the correct guest PKRU value, potentially leading to mismatches and incorrect behavior during execution. The patch resolves this by ensuring the guest PKRU is explicitly used in both the `fill_xsave` and `load_xsave` functions, and prevents loading the host PKRU value in `kvm_load_guest_fpu`.
